(define-memory reauth-opencodex-antigravity-by-pasted-code
  "Re-authenticating an opencodex google-antigravity account on a headless box does not need a browser on that box. Run it inside tmux so it survives turns: `tmux new-session -d -s ocxr 'bash -lc \"export PATH=/home/boxes/.local/bin:$PATH; ocx account reauth google-antigravity --id <id> --accept-antigravity-risk --open-browser off\"'`. Two gates: without `--accept-antigravity-risk` it exits with antigravity_risk_not_acknowledged when stdin is not a terminal, and a run it detects as agent-driven is refused outright, so tmux (a real pty) is what makes it proceed. It then prints 'Open this URL to sign in:' with redirect_uri http://127.0.0.1:51121/callback and waits, saying 'paste the redirect URL or code if prompted' — the operator approves on any device and pastes back the address-bar URL of the failed 127.0.0.1:51121 callback (the code is in the query string). Capture the URL whole with `tmux resize-window -t ocxr -x 1200` then grep 'https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth[^ ]*'; never stitch wrapped lines. `ocx account reauth --code -` reads a short-lived code from stdin as a non-interactive alternative. Note the quarantine flag needsReauth(verify_account) survives `ocx account refresh google-antigravity` — refresh does exchange the token and even prints Gem/Cla quota windows, but only a reauth clears the flag."
  :type :reference)
